cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use florilegium in your work, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: florilegium
abstract: >-
  Procedurally generated Delft-blue page margins for LuaLaTeX. Every petal, leaf, stem and
  arch is a parametric curve computed in Lua while the page is written, and placed by a
  greedy space-filling layout that grows plants to fit the free space on each page. The
  plants and their visitors are species sampled from genomes of botanical traits, the
  headpieces over the sections windows of Gothic tracery sampled from a genome of their
  own, the shells on the ground sampled from a third, and a TikZ library draws the same
  species, windows and shells as pics, in pure TikZ under pdfLaTeX or through Lua under
  LuaLaTeX.
authors:
  - family-names: Raymond
    given-names: Kevin
repository-code: https://github.com/kevinraymond/florilegium
url: https://kevinraymond.github.io/florilegium/
license:
  - MIT
  - LPPL-1.3c
keywords:
  - LaTeX
  - LuaLaTeX
  - Lua
  - TikZ
  - pdfLaTeX
  - generative art
  - procedural generation
  - typography
  - ornament
